  <div class="calc-right">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>How Many MPH is 1 Knot?</h2>
      <p>1 knot = <strong>1.15078 miles per hour</strong>. A knot is one nautical mile per hour. The nautical mile is defined as exactly 1,852 meters (1.852 km), based on one minute of arc of latitude along the Earth's surface.</p>
      <div class="answer-box">
        <div class="answer-row"><span class="answer-lbl">1 knot</span><span class="answer-val">= 1.15078 mph</span></div>
        <div class="answer-row"><span class="answer-lbl">1 knot</span><span class="answer-val">= 1.852 km/h</span></div>
        <div class="answer-row"><span class="answer-lbl">1 knot</span><span class="answer-val">= 0.51444 m/s</span></div>
        <div class="answer-row"><span class="answer-lbl">1 mph</span><span class="answer-val">= 0.86898 knots</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-box">mph = knots × 1.15078 &nbsp;|&nbsp; knots = mph ÷ 1.15078</div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Knots to MPH Conversion Chart</h2>
      <p>Click any row to load into the converter above.</p>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto">
      <table class="ref-tbl">
        <thead><tr><th>Knots</th><th>MPH</th><th>km/h</th><th>Context</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            [1,'1.15','1.85','Light air (Beaufort 1)'],
            [5,'5.75','9.26','Light breeze'],
            [10,'11.51','18.52','Gentle breeze'],
            [15,'17.26','27.78','Moderate breeze'],
